<title>NETHERLANDS: DUTCH SHELL RAISES DIESEL PRICE.</title>
<headline>DUTCH SHELL RAISES DIESEL PRICE.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal Dutch/Shell unit Shell Nederland BV said on Thursday it would raise its retail prices for diesel in the Netherlands by 1.8 cent per litre with effect from Saturday, July 5.</p>
<p>The move reflects changes in international product prices and the value of the dollar against the guilder, the company said. It added that gasoline prices would remain unchanged.</p>
<p>From Saturday the recommended price of diesel at Shell's self-service goes up to 1.516 guilders per litre.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
